premises_and_counterexample {"input_domain":["Default Charge was successfully used; no special ability/item/state callbacks alter the counter.","Both sides remain able to battle; a later ordinary move attempt reaches its normal end-of-action cleanup.","For the repeat example: a legal positive-PP ordinary Electric move is in the user’s current slots, normal gates pass, and a later ally uses legal Instruct after the user’s ordinary action; no special blacklist, locks, switching, fainting or host fault applies."],"ordinary_control":"Immediately after newly setting Charge to 2, reaching that same action’s end leaves it 2; this is distinct from the count-1 clear. Another independent control removes Instruct and still observes the counter clear after the ordinary action.","minimal_counterexample":"Charge succeeds in round n: counter 2, then full round-tail 1. In round n+1 the user performs its normal Electric move: its initial damage reads positive Charge and receives the Charge power multiplier. The normal action end clears counter 1 to 0. A later ally’s Instruct repeats that Electric move in the same round, so the repeat reads 0 and receives no Charge multiplier. A timer-only implementation inferred from WP44 keeps 1 through both actions until the round tail and boosts the repeat incorrectly.","failure_cancel_partial_commit":{"cancellation_or_partial_commitment":"Successful first damage, PP and history stay committed; a later repeat does not undo them. A failed ordinary attempt that reaches the same end cleanup also clears the remaining count. A fault or branch that does not reach the cleanup has no automatic clear guarantee."},"impact":"接受当前原提案的行为差异/具名遗漏及非提出者回源反证；修订范围限定原记录的有效前提、最小规则、正确scope与静态验收，不授运行或永久缺陷兼容。","evidence_levels_and_execution":{"evidence_class":"STATIC_REFERENCE_INSPECTION + DERIVED_VECTOR","execution":"NOT_EXECUTED","isolated_reference_execution":false,"independent_model_execution":false,"full_host_or_demo_execution":false}}
